aking bonds requires energy.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G11","subject":"CHEMISTRY","unit_number":2,"title":"Chemical Equilibrium","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Dynamic equilibrium","body":"Forward and reverse rates equal.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Keq","body":"Products over reactants (concentrations).","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Le Chatelier","body":"System shifts to oppose change.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Worked idea","body":"Add product → shift left.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"Catalyst speeds both directions equally.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G11","subject":"CHEMISTRY","unit_number":3,"title":"Organic Chemistry","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Hydrocarbons","body":"Alkanes CₙH₂ₙ₊₂; alkenes have C=C.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Functional groups","body":"−OH alcohol; −COOH acid; −NH₂ amine.","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Isomers","body":"Same formula, different structure.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Worked idea","body":"C₂H₅OH is ethanol.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"Combustion of hydrocarbons → CO₂ + H₂O.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G11","subject":"BIOLOGY","unit_number":1,"title":"Cell Biology Advanced","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Organelles","body":"Mitochondria ATP; ribosomes protein; nucleus DNA.","accent":"#0D9488"},{"n":2,"heading":"Membrane transport","body":"Diffusion, osmosis, active transport.","accent":"#7C3AED"},{"n":3,"heading":"Mitosis vs meiosis","body":"Growth vs gametes.","accent":"#0284C7"},{"n":4,"heading":"Worked idea","body":"Osmosis: water moves to higher solute.","accent":"#EA580C"},{"n":5,"heading":"Try this","body":"Enzymes are biological catalysts.","accent":"#DB2777"}]},{"grade":"G11","subject":"BIOLOGY","unit_number":2,"title":"Genetics and Evolution","type":"illustrated_cards","slides":[{"n":1,"heading":"Mendel","body":"